# Application rules

## Framework semantics

Application rules (`RulesChecker` via `buildRules()`) check stateful properties during `save()` / `delete()` (e.g. `isUnique`, `existsIn`).

## Required behavior

- Enforce uniqueness and existence with application rules.
- Keep rule failures on the entity error collection.
- Prefer rules over ad-hoc `beforeSave` boolean gates for invariants.

## Anti-patterns

- Encoding uniqueness only in callbacks
- Confusing rules with HTTP validation-only flows

## Review checklist

- [ ] Stateful invariants in `buildRules()`
- [ ] Create/update/delete modes considered when needed